# Public orrery app vhost — ROUTING OWNED BY THIS REPO.
#
# The shared Caddy EDGE ENGINE (install, systemd unit, base Caddyfile, firewall,
# the deploy@ `systemctl restart caddy` sudoers grant) is owned by podcast_scraper
# (ADR-114). The base Caddyfile does `import /etc/caddy/sites/*.caddy`, so this
# tenant vhost is picked up automatically once dropped in. ops/deploy_caddy_vhosts.sh
# installs it into /etc/caddy/sites/orrery.caddy, `caddy adapt`-gates the merged
# config, then `sudo -n systemctl restart caddy`.
#
# Domain: orrerylearn.com (apex) + www.orrerylearn.com. Caddy issues a cert covering
# BOTH names, so BOTH must resolve to the box first — a name without DNS makes ACME
# retry (and can burn LE rate limits). Upstream is orrery's own nginx container on the
# reserved loopback port 8090 (ADR-114 §port map) — fully self-contained, no cross-repo
# coupling.
#
# Rollback: `rm /etc/caddy/sites/orrery.caddy && sudo systemctl restart caddy` —
# frees the vhost, nothing shared changes, the box stays up.
orrerylearn.com www.orrerylearn.com {
	import hardened
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8090
}
